 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "So, I want you to avoid using them in your code.",
  "It's a personal preference for our team, and we've found it works better this way for our projects.",
  "Also, I want you to get into the habit of adding the '@timer_class' decorator from the 'pedantic' module to all your classes.",
  "This is a standard practice we follow here, and it helps with code profiling and performance analysis.",
  "For now, focus on getting comfortable with our coding standards, and don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions.",
  "It's important to stay motivated and keep learning.",
  "I want to emphasize that from now on, I'd like you to use a pre-commit hook for all your code contributions.",
  "Think of it as a safety net.",
  "When you set up a pre-commit hook, it automatically runs checks on your code before allowing you to create a new commit.",
  "These checks can include formatting, linting, and even simple tests.",
  "For our purposes, setting it up locally for this project will be sufficient.",
  "The pre-commit hook is all about catching issues early and ensuring your code is of high quality.",
  "You can include project-specific checks, such as ensuring your code adheres to any unique style guides or best practices we have in place.",
  "It's a great way to develop good habits and maintain a clean code base.",
  "Keep up the good work, and don't be afraid to challenge yourself.",
  "And we can make sure to include some team-building games or activities while we're there.",
  "I want you to get into the habit of adding the '@trace_class' decorator from the 'pedantic' module to all your classes."
 ],
